			<div class="content" id="post-content-944729">
									

<p>Other than the fact that I don't really see how the Jovian magnetosphere can amplify and rebroadcast the signal, I see no scientific problems with it, and I can let this slip. One thing you might want to include is the approximate bandwidth/baud rate to give it a more 'alien' quality: if the baud rate is very high, that triple-digit run time would indicate that it transmits a <em>scary</em> amount of data about humanity.</p>
<p>How about building a BOMB-4 inside a grounded metallic enclosure with the PSU and everything inside? That way, it would be absolutely shielded against EMPs, and we could get the rest of the signal.</p>
<p>And what a coincidence: 1819: <a href="http://rss.slashdot.org/~r/Slashdot/slashdot/~3/ECUPX8Ye4Ng/story01.htm" onclick="window.open(this.href, '_blank'); return false;">Rouge Satellite Shuts Down U.S. Weather Services</a></p>

