			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-945007">
									

<p>A satellite that transmits <em>sensitive</em> data (nukes! satellites!! nukes inside satellites!!!) and apparently doesn't want anyone investigating it too closely is cause for concern all by itself. The fact that it seems to be quite capable of preventing said investigation with some powerfully anomalous measures makes it even more compelling.</p>
<p>As for "something the foundation could easily handle," what strange orifice are you pulling that one out of? It's made pretty clear in the description that this thing has a way of interfering with conventional rocketry, and I can't think of any specific examples of the Foundation's aerospace superiority, aside from a few demon airplanes and that moonbase made out of piled up D Class corpses.</p>
<p>So I put it to you: make a god damned point! And Happy Holidays ☃</p>

